    <statement><p>Find an equation of the tangent plane at the given point:</p>
<p><m>F(r,s)=-\left(3r^{2}\frac{1}{s^{0.5}}+\frac{1}{s^{3}}\right), \qquad (-2,1)</m></p>
<p><m>z=</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>12r+9s+2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>(-2,1)</m> is 
<me>z=f(-2,1)+f_r(-2,1)(r + 2)+f_s(-2,1)(s-1)</me>

We compute the value of the function and its partial derivatives at the point <m>(-2,1)</m>:
<me>\left. \begin{array}{lcl}
f(r,s)=-\left(3r^{2}\frac{1}{s^{0.5}}+\frac{1}{s^{3}}\right) \amp   \amp  f(-2,1)=-13 \\
f_r(r,s)=-6r\frac{1}{s^{0.5}} \amp  \Rightarrow \amp  f_r(-2,1)=12 \\
f_s(r,s)=1.5r^{2}\frac{1}{s^{1.5}}+3\frac{1}{s^{4}} \amp   \amp  f_s(-2,1)=9 \end{array} \right.</me>

We substitute these values to obtain the following equation of the tangent plane:
<me>z=12\mathopen{}\left(r+2\right)-13+9\mathopen{}\left(s-1\right)=12r+9s+2</me>





</solution>
